<item>
  <title>Interacting with the Google Gemini API from Python</title>
  <link>https://dcliff36.github.io/posts/google-gemini-api/google-gemini-api.html</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<section id="what-is-google-gemini" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="what-is-google-gemini">What is Google Gemini?</h2>
<p>Google Gemini is Google’s AI assistant. You can talk to it from Python by sending it a prompt (a question or instruction) and it sends back a response. This post walks through everything you need to get started.</p>
</section>
<section id="step-1-create-a-google-account" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-1-create-a-google-account">Step 1 — Create a Google Account</h2>
<p>If you have Gmail, you already have one. If not, go to <a href="https://accounts.google.com">accounts.google.com</a> and sign up.</p>
</section>
<section id="step-2-get-your-api-key" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-2-get-your-api-key">Step 2 — Get Your API Key</h2>
<ol type="1">
<li>Go to <a href="https://aistudio.google.com">aistudio.google.com</a></li>
<li>Sign in and click <strong>“Get API Key”</strong> → <strong>“Create API Key”</strong></li>
<li>Copy it and save it somewhere safe — treat it like a password</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section id="step-3-store-your-key-safely" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-3-store-your-key-safely">Step 3 — Store Your Key Safely</h2>
<p>Never paste your key directly in the notebook. In your terminal, run:</p>
<div id="19a4249a" class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Run this in your terminal BEFORE opening the notebook (not as a code cell)</span></span>
<span id="cb1-2"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Mac/Linux:  export GEMINI_API_KEY="your-key-here"</span></span>
<span id="cb1-3"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Windows:    set GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here</span></span>
<span id="cb1-4"></span>
<span id="cb1-5"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Install the library</span></span>
<span id="cb1-6"><span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">!</span>pip install google<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>generativeai</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="step-4-connect-to-gemini" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-4-connect-to-gemini">Step 4 — Connect to Gemini</h2>
<div id="a82c0060" class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb2" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb2-1"><span class="im" style="color: #00769E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">import</span> os</span>
<span id="cb2-2"><span class="im" style="color: #00769E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">import</span> google.generativeai <span class="im" style="color: #00769E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">as</span> genai</span>
<span id="cb2-3"></span>
<span id="cb2-4">genai.configure(api_key<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span>os.environ[<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"GEMINI_API_KEY"</span>])</span>
<span id="cb2-5">model <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> genai.GenerativeModel(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"gemini-1.5-flash"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb2-6"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Connected successfully!"</span>)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="step-5-send-prompts" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-5-send-prompts">Step 5 — Send Prompts</h2>
<p>Now we can send questions to Gemini and print the responses.</p>
<div id="c1aa76ba" class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb3-1"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Basic question</span></span>
<span id="cb3-2">response <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> model.generate_content(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"What is machine learning? Explain in 3 sentences."</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-3"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"--- Basic Question ---"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-4"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(response.text)</span>
<span id="cb3-5"></span>
<span id="cb3-6"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Ask it to write code</span></span>
<span id="cb3-7">response <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> model.generate_content(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Write a Python function that calculates the mean of a list."</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-8"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"--- Code Generation ---"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-9"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(response.text)</span>
<span id="cb3-10"></span>
<span id="cb3-11"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Summarize text</span></span>
<span id="cb3-12">text <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Pandas is a Python library for data manipulation. It provides DataFrames for working with tabular data and integrates well with NumPy and Matplotlib."</span></span>
<span id="cb3-13">response <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> model.generate_content(<span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">f"Summarize this in one sentence: </span><span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">{</span>text<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">}</span><span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-14"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"--- Summarization ---"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-15"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(response.text)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="step-6-multi-turn-conversation" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="step-6-multi-turn-conversation">Step 6 — Multi-Turn Conversation</h2>
<p>Gemini can also hold a conversation where it remembers previous messages.</p>
<div id="5960aea1" class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb4" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb4-1">chat <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> model.start_chat(history<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span>[])</span>
<span id="cb4-2"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Turn 1:"</span>, chat.send_message(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"I'm learning Python for data science. Where should I start?"</span>).text)</span>
<span id="cb4-3"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Turn 2:"</span>, chat.send_message(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"What should I learn after Pandas?"</span>).text)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="summary" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="summary">Summary</h2>
<p>In this post we: - Created a Google account and obtained a Gemini API key from AI Studio - Installed <code>google-generativeai</code> and connected to the model safely using an environment variable - Sent basic questions, generated code, summarized text, and held a multi-turn conversation</p>
<p>The free tier is generous — it’s a great tool to experiment with in your data science work.</p>


</section>

 ]]></description>
